Complaints, Vulnerable Customers & Accessibility
9. Financial difficulty
Customers who cannot pay bills, loan repayments, overdrafts, or credit-card balances should contact Aurora Bank as early as possible. Early contact gives more options.
Support may include:
- income and expenditure review;
- temporary payment arrangement;
- overdraft review;
- breathing-space or moratorium process where available;
- referral to free debt advice;
- freezing certain charges where appropriate;
- restructuring or term extension where allowed;
- collections hold while evidence is reviewed.
Financial difficulty support may affect credit reporting depending on the arrangement.

Complaints, Vulnerable Customers & Accessibility
4. What Aurora Bank may do to resolve a complaint
Depending on the facts, Aurora Bank may:
- apologize;
- correct an error;
- refund a fee or interest;
- make a goodwill payment;
- update records;
- reopen an investigation;
- provide staff feedback or training;
- improve a process;
- explain why the original decision was correct;
- refer the customer to an external dispute resolution body.
Aurora Bank does not provide compensation for every inconvenience, and redress depends on evidence, legal obligations, financial loss, distress, and fairness.

Payments, Transfers & Cutoff Times
7. Future-dated payments and standing orders
A future-dated payment is executed on a date chosen by the customer. A standing order is a repeated future-dated payment. The customer must ensure there is enough available balance before the payment is due.
If there is not enough available balance at the processing time, Aurora Bank may:
- reject the payment;
- retry the payment later the same day;
- create or increase an arranged overdraft if available and permitted;
- create an unarranged overdraft only where permitted by product terms.
Rejected-payment fees may apply. See [Fees, Interest & Foreign Exchange](06_fees_interest_and_exchange_rates.md).

Loans, Overdrafts & Credit Assessment
4. Documents for employed customers
Employed customers may be asked for:
- recent payslips;
- employment contract or employer confirmation;
- bank statements showing salary credits;
- tax certificate or annual income statement;
- proof of address;
- details of other credit commitments.
Where salary is paid into an Aurora current account, fewer documents may be required, but Aurora Bank may still request evidence.

Account Opening, Eligibility & Customer Verification Policy
4. Application channels
Customers may apply through:
1. Aurora Online Banking or the mobile application;
2. an Aurora branch or partner branch;
3. telephone-assisted onboarding for customers who need accessibility support;
4. a workplace, student, or relocation onboarding program approved by Aurora Bank.
Online applications can usually be completed without visiting a branch. We may still require branch verification if documents are unclear, fraud indicators are present, or the customer is applying for a product with enhanced checks.

Disputes, Chargebacks & Fraud Claims
9. Payment sent to the wrong account
If a customer authorized a transfer to the wrong IBAN or beneficiary, Aurora Bank cannot simply reverse it. We may attempt a recall through the receiving bank. The recipient may need to consent unless legal rules allow otherwise.
The customer should provide:
- payment date and amount;
- beneficiary IBAN and name entered;
- intended beneficiary details;
- reason for error;
- any communication with the unintended recipient.
Recall fees may apply even if recovery is unsuccessful. See [Fees, Interest & Foreign Exchange](06_fees_interest_and_exchange_rates.md).
